**Describe the bug**
In LoRa explicit header mode, after any transmit the LR2021 no longer
receives packets **larger than the packet it just transmitted**. RX appears
armed and healthy (`startReceive()` returns `RADIOLIB_ERR_NONE`,
instantaneous RSSI reads a normal noise floor, no IRQ flags pending), but
RX_DONE never fires for oversized packets. Smaller packets are still
received, which makes the symptom intermittent and traffic-dependent — in a
mesh-style workload (transmit a ~30 B ACK, then expect a ~60 B packet) the
node effectively goes deaf until something rewrites the packet params.

### Root cause

`LR2021::stageMode(RADIOLIB_RADIO_MODE_TX)` sets the LoRa packet params with
`cfg->transmit.len`. When staging RX, the packet params are only rewritten in
**implicit** header mode:

```cpp
// set implicit mode and expected len if applicable
if((this->headerType == RADIOLIB_LR2021_LORA_HEADER_IMPLICIT) && (modem == RADIOLIB_LR2021_PACKET_TYPE_LORA)) {
  state = setLoRaPacketParams(this->preambleLengthLoRa, this->headerType,
    (this->headerType == RADIOLIB_LR2021_LORA_HEADER_IMPLICIT) ? this->implicitLen : RADIOLIB_LR2021_MAX_PACKET_LENGTH, this->crcTypeLoRa, this->invertIQEnabled);
  RADIOLIB_ASSERT(state);
}
```

<details><summary>EDIT by @jgromes: collapsed LLM fluff</summary>
<p>

So in explicit mode the TX payload length stays in effect. Per the LR20xx
datasheet (same wording as SX126x/LR11x0): PayloadLen is "the size of the
payload to transmit **or the maximum size of the payload that the receiver
can accept**". Note the inner ternary already handles the explicit case with
`RADIOLIB_LR2021_MAX_PACKET_LENGTH` — but it is unreachable behind the
implicit-only condition, so it looks like the fix was intended and the outer
check was just not updated.

This is the same root cause as #298, fixed for SX126x in 2021 — SX126x's RX
staging unconditionally restores the packet length ("restore original packet
length").

```

