When using the `setRxBoostedGainMode` parameter, I noticed that the gain value was not being configured or applied correctly. 
It appears there might be a minor logical issue—or is there perhaps another design consideration at play?


`src\modules\LR2021\LR2021_config.cpp`

```
int16_t LR2021::setRxBoostedGainMode(uint8_t level) {
  int16_t state = this->setRxPath(this->highFreq ? RADIOLIB_LR2021_RX_PATH_HF : RADIOLIB_LR2021_RX_PATH_LF, this->highFreq ? this->gainModeHf : this->gainModeLf);
  RADIOLIB_ASSERT(state);
  if(this->highFreq) {
    this->gainModeHf = level;
  } else {
    this->gainModeLf = level;
  }
  return(state);
}
```
Here, the configuration command is invoked first, utilizing the default values ​​defined within the class rather than the passed-in parameter values; the passed-in parameter values ​​will only be utilized during the subsequent invocation.

This looks more normal.
```
int16_t LR2021::setRxBoostedGainMode(uint8_t level) {
  if(this->highFreq) {
    this->gainModeHf = level;
  } else {
    this->gainModeLf = level;
  }
  int16_t state = this->setRxPath(this->highFreq ? RADIOLIB_LR2021_RX_PATH_HF : RADIOLIB_LR2021_RX_PATH_LF, this->highFreq ? this->gainModeHf : this->gainModeLf);
  RADIOLIB_ASSERT(state);
  return(state);
}
```

**Describe the bug**

This is a follow up for PR https://github.com/jgromes/RadioLib/pull/1751#issuecomment-4275767778

Since the LR2021 module is heavily derived from LR11x0 one,
the issue with enforced `RADIOLIB_LR11X0_MAX_PACKET_LENGTH` value for `setPacketParamsGFSK` still remains in the  LR11x0 module source code as well:

